    <!-- Siege Tank Spider Mines (AP): lay a cloaked Vulture spider mine. Modeled on the
         vanilla VultureSpiderMines ability. IgnoreFacing is REQUIRED: a SIEGED tank cannot
         turn, so without it the deploy fails with "Can't turn towards target".
         #11 fix: the effect was SpawnSpiderMineSet = [SpawnSpiderMine,
         ReplenishNanoConstructor]. ReplenishNanoConstructor is a CEffectModifyUnit with
         Cost Abil="MakeVultureSpiderMines,Specialize1" ChargeCountUse="-1" — it tries to
         refund a charge on the Vulture-only MakeVultureSpiderMines ability, which a tank /
         siege breaker doesn't have. On the SIEGED form that broken refund aborts the set so
         no mine spawns (mobile mode tolerated it). Our ability uses a 1 s cooldown, not the
         Vulture charge system, so the replenish is unnecessary: point Effect at the raw
         SpawnSpiderMine create alone. The mine still spawns + burrows (CEffectCreateUnit
         spawns the SpiderMine unit, whose own AI burrows on idle). Button gated WoLUHaveFlag,
         appended to the tanks (enemy-invisible); SpiderMineWoLU face = own hotkey (#10). -->
    <CAbilEffectTarget id="SpiderMineWoLU">
        <EditorCategories value="Race:Terran,AbilityorEffectType:Units"/>
        <Effect index="0" value="SpawnSpiderMine"/>
        <Placeholder value="SpiderMine"/>
        <Range value="4"/>
        <Flags index="IgnoreFacing" value="1"/>
        <Cost>
            <Cooldown TimeUse="1"/>
        </Cost>
        <CmdButtonArray index="Execute" DefaultButtonFace="SpiderMineWoLU" Requirements="WoLUHaveFlag"/>
    </CAbilEffectTarget>

